 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 # Types: observe, decide, surprise, revise, blocked, taste, rebase, hygiene, implement, verify, note
 >>[2026-03-26 00:00] observe — completion is still dominated by static sigil snippets, root paths, and annotation names while register and workspace signals remain mostly passive.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:01] observe — code lens already computes useful runtime and projection summaries, but none of those surfaces are currently actionable.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:02] decide — the first authoring-loop slice should keep the terminal harness intact and concentrate on command routing plus richer editor affordances.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:03] hygiene — original branch memory recorded main@f42a80fa8eefb813992e21f7461c96926f033416 at plan time.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:04] hygiene — local drift is present in annotation-index.ts, extension.ts, and stdio-server.ts; implementation should isolate that work before commit 1.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:05] taste — status surfaces should accelerate attention, not become a second dashboard inside the editor chrome.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:06] revise — broaden the authoring loop to account for theming nuance, formatting/refactor flows, graph-query probes, and perspective rotations during inspection.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:07] revise — relax the plan from atlas/register-last sequencing to additive composition. The authoring loop now needs a solo-ship path from local parse/runtime context, with atlas/register data treated as optional enrichments.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:08] observe — phase-aware completion's look-back rule needs AST-precise spirit-sequence context at cursor offset. The seed parser does not currently expose this.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:09] decide — note seed_phase_context as an unscoped enrichment. Solo ship uses regex look-back; AST-precise phase detection is a later seed parser addition.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:10] observe — runtime-telemetry-canon enriches probe results with substrate events and resonances. Without it, probe.completed carries shallow results.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:11] decide — acknowledge runtime-telemetry-canon as a cross-theme enrichment, not a blocker. Solo ship probes return basic results; enriched probes arrive when telemetry-canon is present.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:12] observe — the two phase axes (spirit-sequence vs pipeline) need explicit disambiguation in authoring surfaces. In completions and status bar, phase means spirit-sequence.
 >>[2026-03-27 14:38] revise — regrounded branch baseline to current planning canon main@3b1747c4 so the authoring lane speaks the same packages-era lineage as the other active editor/runtime plans.
 >>[2026-03-27 14:39] implement — rewrote branch memory with roots, concept indexing, and recursive improvement so authoring work can be queried as a learning surface instead of a raw feature list.
 >>[2026-03-27 18:00] revise — rooted into register-bank.spw, literate-architecture.spw, dialect-spec.spw, editing handler, and runtime RegisterBank. Added parallel_work (LSP integration provides semantic surface, atlas provides workspace context, register explorer provides focused register), supporting_documents (interaction contract, register spec, spirit sequence, module shape, keyboard nav, interaction design), interaction_depth, and cognitive_surface_stack. This plan operates at the register layer: phase-aware completion reads spirit-sequence from register-bank, materialization breadcrumb reads literate-architecture stages, operator heat echoes register-bank acoustic properties, probes read Substrate events. The authoring loop is where syntax-as-navigation from literate-ui becomes cursor-local editorial experience.
 >>[2026-03-28 09:47] rebase — refreshed baseline to main@b41caa6b and added references/index.spw so programmatic-language features, commands, quick-picks, status-bar, and tree-view guidance are attached to authoring-surface judgments instead of carried as lore.
 >>[2026-03-28 10:18] observe — the March 26, 2026 VS Code implementation log establishes a thin-client baseline: standard language features moved into the LSP, the extension shell stayed small, and the only custom surface still in the client is the Concepts tree plus the LSP-backed annotation mirror. The authoring plan should spend budget on semantics, cheap continuous feedback, and probe flow, not on reviving provider-era client logic.
 >>[2026-03-28 10:19] revise — local drift noted on 2026-03-26 is absent in the current clean worktree. Keep extension.ts, context.ts, package.json, and stdio-server.ts treated as shared hot files, but drop the mandatory hygiene split until fresh drift appears.
 >>[2026-03-29 01:00] observe — vscode-lsp-integration archived with 80 handler tests. SpwContext, EventBus, and custom request infrastructure confirmed working. All shared substrate for authoring is in place.
 >>[2026-03-29 01:01] decide — added Performance Considerations and Implementation Notes to PLAN.md: cursor-movement debounce (50ms), phase look-back via regex O(line-length), no full-reparse on keystroke, status bar items created once in activate(), operator-frequency heat as on-demand command only, probe via spw/probe custom request. New files: runtime-status.ts (~2 StatusBarItems), probe-commands.ts (~3 commands). Existing handler modifications: editing.ts (~30 lines for phase ranking), display.ts (~20 lines for hover), analysis.ts (~40 lines for materialization lens).
 >>[2026-07-20 19:31] revise — operational-topography supersedes regex-owned phase truth and client-local formatter semantics; authoring consumes exact selections, evidence grades, transform profiles, and verified differential previews.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:32] observe — spw/probe remains unimplemented and unadvertised, and prior latency assertions were estimates without actual-path traces; protocol and performance evidence precede commands.
 >>[2026-07-20 19:33] decide — learner babble may use S0/S1 preview sandboxes; idiom promotion and any S2 pattern migration require exact impact packets and steward review.
 >>[2026-07-21] observe — form-geometry mobility/HOF and pulse CLI land; authoring should consume form-geometry-editor actions rather than invent client geometry.
 >>[2026-07-21] decide — prioritize formContext + mobility code actions over phantom phaseContext/operatorFrequency until those methods are earned for a hard surface need.
 >>[2026-10-12 12:47] observe — Consumer review (pin 229aedcf): stream entries need a manifest-clock stamp, entry hover and order diagnostics; plan folders need status, gate and the wonder question in hover; triggers should act at typing, creating, saving and index-ready, never on a timer. Re-checked on main: the stream snippet still asks for a typed timestamp. Added as PLAN.md slices; the card stays dormant until re-scoped against a999a24f.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:53] note — Received rehomed intents from command-experience-tools: rehomed_intents frame, two open questions, commits 7 and 8.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:55] decide — User decided 2026-10-12 to reheat this plan from dormant to planning. First slice is stamp completion after the stream marker, served by spw-lsp from the manifest clock.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:32] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 1 landed, 7 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:43] revise — Added stream_stamp_completion as the first planned commit; the card named it as the first slice when the plan was reheated, but no commit line carried it.
 >>[2026-10-12 20:09] implement — Landed in e6c56978: after >>[ the server offers the stamp on the workspace clock, then the eleven stream types; Neovim and IntelliJ get it through the same server.
 >>[2026-10-12 21:02] decide — Planned ~[keyed_value_completion]: after #:key #!, offer the values seen after that key, with counts, instead of every annotation name.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:59] revise — The first slice landed as stream_stamp_completion (e6c56978). code_lens_commands becomes the one owner of lens actions in every host: the executeCommand route was claimed in four places (this plan, citation-navigation lens_reference_peek, apposition-cache-granules granule_codelens, and 99e6d993 outside any plan). The probe and run commands already exist, so probe_run_commands narrows to operator-frequency heat.
 >>[2026-10-13 20:52] revise — hole_fill_actions planned: the owner saw an inline completer propose 0x0bso is hex, which the parser refutes (0 then x0bso); a fill an agent proposes is kept only if it parses in place and its checkable claims hold.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] note — A mounted consumer asks (2026-10-25, rank 13, compare_in_the_editor) for a lens on follows and on a shape members line that compares a sibling, ground first then the edge by slot, in a read-only document; and Compare with in the explorer for any two .spw files. It waits on a CLI ground reading, which the consumer filed as ground_then_edge and which has no home here yet; the generated-file banner actions (rank 12) are the first lenses that act and belong to code_lens_commands.
 >>[2026-10-25 21:33] note — Server code lenses now carry their own client commands with JSON arguments (spw.showLocations, spw.openUri, spw.rebuildGenerated; uncommitted 2026-10-25), so the title-matching reference peek in the extension matches no server lens and can retire under code_lens_commands. There is still no workspace/executeCommand route, so these lenses do nothing in Neovim.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:24] observe — The lens commands noted at 2026-10-25 21:33 as uncommitted landed in 55e79d2e: citation lenses carry spw.showLocations with their sites, and the generated banner carries spw.openUri and spw.rebuildGenerated, each registered by the VS Code client only. The server still has no executeCommandProvider and the title-matching peek in code-lens-middleware.ts still stands, so code_lens_commands keeps its scope. phase_completion_hover moves below code_lens_commands, matching the card, which re-scopes it against formContext before it is next.
}

